---"
"3612","Chapter: Mentioning the evidence that applying perfume after stoning the Jamaraat, slaughtering the sacrificial animal, and shaving the head is merely permissible according to some scholars before visiting the House (Tawaf al-Ifadah) for those who have already performed Tawaf around the House before standing at Arafah, as opposed to those who have not performed Tawaf around the House before standing at Arafah."
"3613","Muhammad bin Al-Ala' bin Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb (meaning the son of Ishaq) narrated to us, from Hisham (who is the son of Urwah), from Umm Az-Zubayr, the daughter of Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, that she informed him, from A'isha, the daughter of Abdur-Rahman and his sister, that 'Abbad bin Abdillah..."
"3614","**
Narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Tamīmī (RA): It was said, ""What completes the Hajj of the pilgrim?"" He replied, ""Fear that something may befall him which would prevent him from performing the Tawāf al-Zīyārah (the Farewell Tawāf) with it. Even though delaying the Ifāḍah (the departure from Minā) until after the Day of Nahr (the 10th of Dhū al-Ḥijjah) is permissible."""
"3615","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi`, who said: Narrated to us `Abd al-Razzaq, who said: News came to us from `Ubayd Allah, from Nafi`, from Ibn `Umar (RA)."
"3616","I read to Ahmad bin Abi Suraif ar-Razi that Amr bin Mujammi' al-Kindi informed them, on the authority of Musa bin 'Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:"
"3617","**
