We entered upon Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, and he mentioned the hadith at length. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) proceeded to the House — meaning on the Day of Sacrifice — and came to the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib as they were drawing water from Zamzam. He said:

---"
"3619","Narrated to us Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala', who narrated to us Sufyan (Sufyan al-Thawri), who narrated to us Asim (Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud), on the authority of al-Sha'bi (Amr ibn Sharahil al-Sha'bi), on the authority of Ibn Abbas (Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him). *Note: The provided source text only includes the narration chain (isnad) and does not contain the actual content (matn) of the hadith.*"
"3620","The Prophet (ﷺ) had already informed them that this was a righteous deed, and he informed them that had it not been for the fear that the one drawing water from the well would be overwhelmed by those drawing water, he would have drawn water with them."
"3621","Abu Bishr al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to the water station (Saqiyah) and asked for a drink. Al-Abbas said: ""O Fadl, go to your mother and bring the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a drink from her."" He said:"
"3622","###
 Muhammad bin Aban narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd al-Tawil, from Bakr bin Abdullah. And also, Abu Bisr al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, from Bakr. This is the narration of Ibn Abi Adi:

An Arab Bedouin came to the water station (serving drinks) and drank *Nabidh* (a lightly fermented"
"3623","**
Narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la, who said: Ibn Wahb informed us, who said: Malik informed him.

Also narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari, who said: Muhammad (meaning Ibn Ja'far) Ghundar informed us, who said: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah (RA) that she said:

---"
"3624","Abu Bakr said: The statement of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it” is indicative, and the consensus of all Muslims However, if a forgetful person forgets an obligatory prayer and remembers it after Fajr or after Asr, he must pray it before sunrise. He mentioned it after the morning, and before sunset, if he mentioned it after the afternoon; Because “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only forbade voluntary prayers after Fajr, before sunrise, and after Asr, before sunset.” If he had forbidden all prayers, whether obligatory or voluntary, it would not have been permissible to perform an obligatory prayer after Fajr, before sunrise, or after the afternoon prayer. Before sunset, and if he forgot about it, then he mentioned it at one of these two times. The second proof is that he only wanted to do some voluntary work, not All of them, I will explain it in its appropriate place in this book, God willing."
"3625","**
Narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā al-Tamīmī (RA): I said to Mālik ibn Anas (RA), ""Inform me of a concise report that does not go into excessive detail, and provide evidence that there is no fidyah (ransom) for it."""
"3626","**
Narrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala' and Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, they said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from al-Zuhri, from 'Isa ibn Talhah, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr (RA), who said:
""A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr) and said, 'I have shaved my head before slaughtering.'"""
"3627","**
Narrated to us Bishr ibn Mu‘ādh al-‘Aqadī and al-Sana‘ānī (may Allah have mercy upon them), they said: Narrated to us Yazīd ibn Zuray‘: Narrated to us Khālid, from ‘Ikrimah, from Ibn ‘Abbās (RA), who said:
The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked on the Day of Sacrifice at Minā, so he said:

---"
"3628","Ali bin Khashram narrated to us, Isa bin Yunus informed us, from Ibn Jurayj. [This is a supporting (mutaba'ah) chain for the following narration, which is also transmitted via a second independent chain:] Muhammad bin Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ibn Shihab az-Zuhri state: Isa bin Talha narrated to me, that Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), while he was delivering the sermon on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm an-Nahr), a man stood up before him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I never thought that such and such would occur before such and such."" Then another man stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I never thought that such and such would occur before such and such for these three [matters]."" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: [the provided Arabic narration cuts off mid-sentence at this point, with no further text included in the source material provided]."
"3629","**
Abu Bakrah (RA) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon on the day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr), and the hadith is lengthy.

Narrated to us Bundar, who said: narrated to us Abu 'Amir, who said: narrated to us Qurrah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, and Humaid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakrah (RA)."
"3630","**
Narrated to us 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-'Azim al-'Anbari, who said: Narrated to us al-Nadr ibn Muhammad, who said: Narrated to us 'Ikrimah—he is the son of 'Ammar—who said: Narrated to us al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad al-Bahili, who said:

---"
"3631","**
Narrated to us Ar-Rabee', who said: Narrated to us Bashsh ibn Bakr, on the authority of Al-Awzaa'ee, who said: Muhammad ibn Ibraaheem ibn Al-Haarith At-Taymee narrated to me, who said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, who said: 'Aa'ishah (RA) narrated to me, who said:

""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the ifaadah (i.e., the Farewell Tawaaf), then he wanted from Safiyyah what a man wants from his wife. It was said to him, 'She is menstruating.' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:

---"
"3632","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to me 'Amr ibn 'Asim, narrated to me Abu al-'Awwam — and his name is 'Imran ibn Dawud al-Qattan — narrated to me Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Ziyad ibn 'Ilqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik (RA), who said:
""I witnessed the Prophet (ﷺ) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, while he was delivering a sermon. A man came and said, 'I forgot to throw the pebbles (during the stoning ritual).'""

---"
"3633","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashaj narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalid, meaning Sulaiman bin Hassan, narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha (RA), who said:"
