"3637","**
Narrated to us 'Abdul-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala' and Sa'id ibn 'Abd ar-Rahman, they said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from az-Zuhri, from Abu 'Ubayd— and al-Makhzumi said: the freed slave of Ibn Azhar—he said: I witnessed the 'Eid prayer with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (RA), so he said:

""Indeed, this is a day which Allah has made a celebration for the Muslims. So when you come to prayer, come with tranquility, dignity, and solemnity. And when the prayer is completed, then disperse among the people.""

---"
"3638","**
